{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-js","path":"/posts/webmcp-exposing-your-web-app-tools-to-browser-agents/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 1280px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/00711/hero.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 33.4375%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/fb34c/hero.avif 320w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/646cd/hero.avif 768w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/8b485/hero.avif 1024w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/a73d6/hero.avif 1280w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/a7f9f/hero.avif 1920w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/fb732/hero.avif 2400w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n              type=\"image/avif\"\n            /><source\n              srcset=\"/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/cb523/hero.webp 320w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/cd067/hero.webp 768w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/53334/hero.webp 1024w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/4b075/hero.webp 1280w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/f3ff0/hero.webp 1920w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/4293a/hero.webp 2400w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/d4f27/hero.png 320w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/778aa/hero.png 768w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/658fc/hero.png 1024w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/26c69/hero.png 1280w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/7d442/hero.png 1920w,\n/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/00711/hero.png 2400w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/eeaef326d4b6df4ab9a3d2a8deeb76d0/26c69/hero.png\"\n            alt=\"hero\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>TL;DR; WebMCP lets your page register tools (<code class=\"language-text\">name</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">description</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">inputSchema</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">execute</code>) with <code class=\"language-text\">document.modelContext.registerTool()</code>, so a browser agent calls your code instead of clicking around your UI. It's a proposal in an origin trial, so ship it as a progressive enhancement and keep anything consequential behind the user. 🎉</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><em>This post is part of my series \"AI on the web in 2026\". Everything below describes a <strong>proposal</strong>: API names and behaviour may change before anything ships by default.</em></p>\n<h3>Introduction</h3>\n<p>Browser agents got good at \"actuation\" this year: reading the DOM or a screenshot, then clicking and typing as if they were the user. It works, until it doesn't. A custom date picker, a multi-step wizard, a button whose label only makes sense to humans, and the agent is guessing.</p>\n<p>Neither side is happy. The agent is slow and brittle, and you have no say in how it uses your app.</p>\n<p><strong>WebMCP flips that: the page tells the agent what it can do, and your own code does it.</strong></p>\n<p>In this post, I'll cover what WebMCP is, the current API shape (imperative and declarative), where it runs today, how Angular supports it, and the security rules I'd follow before exposing a single tool.</p>\n<h3>What is WebMCP?</h3>\n<p>WebMCP is a proposal from the W3C Web Machine Learning Community Group. Its spec is a Draft Community Group Report, which means it is <strong>not</strong> on the W3C standards track yet.</p>\n<p>The explainer describes pages that use WebMCP as in-page MCP servers: instead of exposing a backend API to an AI platform, the page exposes client-side JavaScript as tools. The difference matters:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Same session, same state.</strong> The tool runs in the page, with the user's existing login and UI state. No second backend to replicate auth for.</li>\n<li><strong>Visible results.</strong> The page updates its UI as the tool runs, so the user sees what the agent did.</li>\n<li><strong>Complement, not replacement.</strong> The explainer lists replacing backend MCP integrations and fully autonomous, headless workflows as non-goals. It's designed for a human in the loop.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Where it stands in November 2026</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Chrome</strong>: an origin trial is live from Chrome 149. For local development, enable <code class=\"language-text\">chrome://flags/#enable-webmcp-testing</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Edge</strong>: an origin trial is live in Edge 150.</li>\n<li><strong>Firefox and Safari</strong>: standards-position discussions are open, with no implementation listed.</li>\n<li><strong>Tooling</strong>: TypeScript types in the <code class=\"language-text\">webmcp-types</code> package, a polyfill in <code class=\"language-text\">@w3c/webmcp-polyfill</code>, and a WebMCP view in Chrome DevTools to inspect registered tools.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you read articles from earlier in the year, you may see <code class=\"language-text\">navigator.modelContext</code> or <code class=\"language-text\">provideContext()</code>. The current spec and Chrome docs use <code class=\"language-text\">document.modelContext.registerTool()</code>, which is what I'll use here.</p>\n<h3>Step 1 — Register an imperative tool</h3>\n<p>Here is a plain JavaScript example for a store. One tool only reads, the other one changes state:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"javascript\"><pre class=\"language-javascript\"><code class=\"language-javascript\"><span class=\"token comment\">// Proposal-stage API: feature-detect and treat it as progressive enhancement.</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'modelContext'</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">in</span> document<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> controller <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">AbortController</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> document<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>modelContext<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">registerTool</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"token literal-property property\">name</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'search_products'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      <span class=\"token literal-property property\">description</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'Searches the catalog and shows matching products on the page.'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      <span class=\"token literal-property property\">inputSchema</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"token literal-property property\">type</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'object'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n        <span class=\"token literal-property property\">properties</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n          <span class=\"token literal-property property\">query</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">type</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'string'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">description</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'Search keywords.'</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n          <span class=\"token literal-property property\">maxPrice</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">type</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'number'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">description</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'Optional maximum price.'</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n        <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n        <span class=\"token literal-property property\">required</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token string\">'query'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      <span class=\"token literal-property property\">annotations</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">readOnlyHint</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token boolean\">true</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">async</span> <span class=\"token function\">execute</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> query<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> maxPrice <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> signal <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> results <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> <span class=\"token function\">searchCatalog</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>query<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> maxPrice<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> signal <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"token function\">renderResults</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>results<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// the user sees the same results the agent gets</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token constant\">JSON</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">stringify</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>results<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">map</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> id<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> name<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> price <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> id<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> name<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> price <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">signal</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> controller<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>signal <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> document<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>modelContext<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">registerTool</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token literal-property property\">name</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'add_to_cart'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token literal-property property\">description</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'Adds a product to the cart. Does not check out.'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token literal-property property\">inputSchema</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"token literal-property property\">type</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'object'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      <span class=\"token literal-property property\">properties</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">productId</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">type</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'string'</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">quantity</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">type</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'number'</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      <span class=\"token literal-property property\">required</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token string\">'productId'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token literal-property property\">annotations</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token literal-property property\">consequentialHint</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token boolean\">true</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">async</span> <span class=\"token function\">execute</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> productId<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> quantity <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token number\">1</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> cart<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">add</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>productId<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> quantity<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// your existing code path, with its validation</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token template-string\"><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span><span class=\"token string\">Added </span><span class=\"token interpolation\"><span class=\"token interpolation-punctuation punctuation\">${</span>quantity<span class=\"token interpolation-punctuation punctuation\">}</span></span><span class=\"token string\"> x </span><span class=\"token interpolation\"><span class=\"token interpolation-punctuation punctuation\">${</span>productId<span class=\"token interpolation-punctuation punctuation\">}</span></span><span class=\"token string\"> to the cart.</span><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token comment\">// Later, when this view goes away:</span>\n  <span class=\"token comment\">// controller.abort();</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>As you can see, there's nothing exotic. The tool reuses the same functions your buttons already call, and the JSON Schema tells the agent exactly what to pass.</p>\n<p>The <code class=\"language-text\">annotations</code> are hints for the agent and the browser: <code class=\"language-text\">readOnlyHint</code> for tools without side effects, <code class=\"language-text\">consequentialHint</code> for significant or non-reversible actions (so the agent or browser can ask the user to confirm), and <code class=\"language-text\">untrustedContentHint</code> when the output contains user-generated or external content. The <code class=\"language-text\">execute</code> function also receives a <code class=\"language-text\">signal</code>, so cancelling a tool can cancel its <code class=\"language-text\">fetch()</code> calls too.</p>\n<h3>Step 2 — Or annotate a form</h3>\n<p>For simple cases, the declarative API turns an existing <code class=\"language-text\">&lt;form></code> into a tool with attributes:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"html\"><pre class=\"language-html\"><code class=\"language-html\"><span class=\"token comment\">&lt;!-- Proposal-stage attributes --></span>\n<span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>form</span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">toolname</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>request_support<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">tooldescription</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>Submits a customer support request.<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">action</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>/support<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n  <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>label</span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">for</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>email<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>Email<span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>label</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n  <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>input</span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">id</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>email<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">name</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>email<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">type</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>email<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">required</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">/></span></span>\n  <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>select</span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">name</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>topic<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">toolparamdescription</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>Which team should handle the request.<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n    <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>option</span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">value</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>returns<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>Return my purchase<span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>option</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n    <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>option</span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">value</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>shipping<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>Where is my package?<span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>option</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n  <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>select</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n  <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>button</span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">type</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>submit<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>Send<span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>button</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>form</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>When an agent calls it, the browser focuses the form and fills the fields, and the user still clicks <strong>Send</strong>. Adding <code class=\"language-text\">toolautosubmit</code> lets the agent submit, and the <code class=\"language-text\">SubmitEvent</code> gets an <code class=\"language-text\">agentInvoked</code> flag plus <code class=\"language-text\">respondWith()</code> to return a result. My default: leave <code class=\"language-text\">toolautosubmit</code> off for anything that matters.</p>\n<h3>Step 3 — In Angular</h3>\n<p>Angular has experimental WebMCP support, explicitly marked as subject to change even outside major versions. Tools can be registered per route, which fits how I'd scope them anyway:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"typescript\"><pre class=\"language-typescript\"><code class=\"language-typescript\"><span class=\"token comment\">// routes.ts (experimental Angular API)</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> inject<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> provideExperimentalWebMcpTools <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'@angular/core'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> Routes <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'@angular/router'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> OrdersService <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'./orders.service'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> routes<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> Routes <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    path<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'orders'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token function-variable function\">loadComponent</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token keyword\">import</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'./orders'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">then</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>m<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> m<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>Orders<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    providers<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>\n      <span class=\"token function\">provideExperimentalWebMcpTools</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>\n        <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n          name<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'getOrderStatus'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n          description<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'Returns the status of one of the signed-in user’s orders.'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n          inputSchema<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n            type<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'object'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n            properties<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> orderId<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> type<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'string'</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n            required<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token string\">'orderId'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n            additionalProperties<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token boolean\">false</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n          <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n          <span class=\"token comment\">// Runs in an injection context, so `inject()` works here.</span>\n          <span class=\"token function-variable function\">execute</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">async</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> orderId <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n            <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> status <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> <span class=\"token function\">inject</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>OrdersService<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">statusFor</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>orderId<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n            <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> content<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> type<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'text'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> text<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token template-string\"><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span><span class=\"token string\">Order </span><span class=\"token interpolation\"><span class=\"token interpolation-punctuation punctuation\">${</span>orderId<span class=\"token interpolation-punctuation punctuation\">}</span></span><span class=\"token string\">: </span><span class=\"token interpolation\"><span class=\"token interpolation-punctuation punctuation\">${</span>status<span class=\"token interpolation-punctuation punctuation\">}</span></span><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n          <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n        <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Pair it with <code class=\"language-text\">provideRouter(routes, withAutoCleanupInjectors())</code>, otherwise route tools stay registered after the user navigates away. Angular also infers <code class=\"language-text\">execute</code> parameter types from the schema, but it doesn't validate the arguments at runtime, so check them yourself. If you use Signal Forms, there's an experimental option to expose a form as a tool too, which pairs nicely with <a href=\"/posts/signal-forms-and-gemini-ai-assisted-form-filling-that-still-validates/\">AI-assisted form filling that still validates</a>.</p>\n<h3>Security: the rules I'd follow</h3>\n<p>The Chrome team's security guidance is honest about it: models are probabilistic, and indirect prompt injection is real. So the safety has to live in your code, not in the description text.</p>\n<h4>1. Expose safe actions first</h4>\n<p>Start with read-only tools and reversible actions. Checkout, deleting data and changing account settings stay with the user, or behind <code class=\"language-text\">consequentialHint</code> plus your own confirmation UI.</p>\n<h4>2. Same session, same rules</h4>\n<p>A tool runs with the user's identity, so it must go through the same authorization and server-side validation as a click. Never add an \"agent-only\" shortcut that skips checks. For anything that acts beyond the page, see <a href=\"/posts/agents-acting-for-users-delegation-oauth-scopes-a2a-and-ap2/\">delegation with OAuth scopes</a>.</p>\n<h4>3. Keep tools on your origin</h4>\n<p>Registration is gated by the <code class=\"language-text\">tools</code> Permissions Policy, which defaults to <code class=\"language-text\">self</code>. Only use <code class=\"language-text\">allow=\"tools\"</code> on iframes or the <code class=\"language-text\">exposedTo</code> option for origins you would share that data with anyway.</p>\n<h4>4. Label untrusted output</h4>\n<p>If a tool returns reviews, comments or third-party data, set <code class=\"language-text\">untrustedContentHint</code>, and keep outputs short. Chrome suggests budgets like 500 characters per tool description and 1.5K per tool output.</p>\n<h4>5. Never return secrets</h4>\n<p>Return what the agent needs to continue, not tokens, internal IDs or someone else's data.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A WebMCP tool is a button with a JSON Schema. Give it the same permissions, validation and review you'd give the button 🔐</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>What this gives you</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Reliability</strong>: agents call a function instead of guessing at the DOM.</li>\n<li><strong>Control</strong>: you decide which actions exist and how they're described.</li>\n<li><strong>Reuse</strong>: tools wrap the client code you already have.</li>\n<li><strong>Progressive enhancement</strong>: feature-detect, and the page keeps working for everyone else.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Before registering tools, measure the basics too: <a href=\"/posts/chrome-devtools-mcp-letting-agents-measure-your-core-web-vitals/\">Chrome DevTools MCP</a> helps check that the page stays fast, and the <a href=\"/posts/frontend-in-the-ai-era-scaling-apps-from-prompt-to-prod/\">talk recap on guardrails</a> covers the accountability side.</p>\n<h3>References &#x26; Further Reading</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">WebMCP explainer (webmachinelearning/webmcp)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">WebMCP specification draft</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp/blob/main/implementation-status.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">WebMCP implementation status</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">WebMCP on Chrome for Developers</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Imperative API</a> and <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Declarative API</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/secure-tools\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Build secure WebMCP tools</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://angular.dev/ai/webmcp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">WebMCP in Angular</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Model Context Protocol</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>That’s all for now</h3>\n<p>WebMCP is still a proposal, and I expect the API to keep moving. But the idea is the right one: describe your app's actions on purpose, instead of hoping an agent reads your UI correctly. Stay tuned because this is not the end, it's just the beginning.</p>\n<p>I hope you enjoyed this reading as much as I enjoyed writing it. Thank you so much for reading until the end and see you soon!</p>\n<p>🚀🚀🚀🚀🚀🚀</p>\n<hr />\n<h3>Cya 👋</h3>","frontmatter":{"date":"November 23, 2026","path":"/posts/webmcp-exposing-your-web-app-tools-to-browser-agents/","title":"WebMCP — exposing your web app tools to browser agents","tags":["ai","web","chrome","javascript","angular","security"],"status":"active"},"timeToRead":6}},"pageContext":{"postPath":"/posts/webmcp-exposing-your-web-app-tools-to-browser-agents/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["1271460761","63159454"],"slicesMap":{}}